  "service": "AlloyDB",
  "title": "AlloyDB Express Clusters & Observability Changes",
  "summary": "AlloyDB v1alpha now supports creating Express clusters. Be aware of breaking changes: several observability and query insights fields on `Instance` are now read-only, becoming output-only information.",
  "details": "A significant update introduces support for AlloyDB Express clusters. You can now enable this feature by setting the new `expressConfig` property on the `Cluster` resource, which includes an `enabled` boolean field within the new `ExpressConfig` schema.\n\n**Breaking Change Alert**: Many properties related to observability and query insights have been made read-only. Specifically, the `observabilityInstanceInfo` and `queryInsightsInfo` properties within the `Instance` schema, along with all their sub-properties in the `ObservabilityInstanceInfo` and `QueryInsightsInstanceInfo` schemas, are now output-only. If your existing code attempts to set these fields during instance creation or updates, it will now fail. You must update your API calls to remove any configuration of these fields.\n\nAdditionally, the `trackActiveQueryPlan` property within the `ObservabilityInstanceInfo` schema is now officially deprecated. Developers should migrate to using `trackActiveQueries` instead.",
  "impact": "high",
  "breaking": true,
  "interesting_score": 9,
